Moby Language II, Grady Ward

Public Domain material by grant from the author, January, 2001.

Source: https://www.gutenberg.org/files/3206/files.zip
Documentation: https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/3206/pg3206.txt

The original public-domain vocabulary is redistributed as normalized word sets.
French, German, Italian and Spanish are included. The normalization removes
ASCII accent notation rather than reconstructing accents. German retains the
source ae/oe/ue spellings; Spanish backslash-n notation is reduced to n.
This is a validity vocabulary, not a spelling-correction dictionary.
Source and derived SHA256 identities are in moby_manifest.json.
